  "term": "card-sorting test",
  "definition": "In assessment, a card-sorting test is a neuropsychological measure used to evaluate executive function, particularly abilities often linked to the frontal lobe such as abstract thinking and strategic planning. The person sorts numbered response cards by different principles and is expected to change strategy during the task.",
